{
  "maps": [
    {
      "id": "laws-of-motion",
      "subject": "Physics",
      "icon": "🚀",
      "title": {
        "en": "Laws of Motion",
        "ta": "இயக்க விதிகள்"
      },
      "blurb": {
        "en": "Force, inertia, momentum, torque and gravitation — one connected picture.",
        "ta": "விசை, நிலைமம், உந்தம், முறுக்கு விசை மற்றும் ஈர்ப்பியல் — ஒரே இணைந்த படம்."
      },
      "createdAt": "2026-09-10T00:00:00Z",
      "root": {
        "id": "root",
        "icon": "🎯",
        "label": {
          "en": "Laws of Motion",
          "ta": "இயக்க விதிகள்"
        },
        "summary": {
          "en": "Force is the cause of changes in the motion of a body. Newton's laws explain how force, motion, momentum and acceleration are related.",
          "ta": "ஒரு பொருளின் இயக்க மாற்றத்திற்குக் காரணம் விசை. விசை, இயக்கம், உந்தம் மற்றும் முடுக்கம் இவற்றின் தொடர்பை நியூட்டனின் விதிகள் விளக்குகின்றன."
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "mechanics",
            "accent": "blue",
            "icon": "⚙️",
            "side": "left",
            "label": {
              "en": "Mechanics",
              "ta": "இயந்திரவியல்"
            },
            "summary": {
              "en": "The branch of physics that studies the effect of forces on bodies.",
              "ta": "பொருட்கள் மீது விசைகளின் விளைவை ஆராயும் இயற்பியலின் பிரிவு."
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "statics",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Statics",
                  "ta": "நிலையியல்"
                },
                "summary": "Deals with bodies at rest.",
                "points": [
                  "Studies bodies under the action of forces in equilibrium.",
                  "The resultant force on the body is zero."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "dynamics",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Dynamics",
                  "ta": "இயக்கவியல்"
                },
                "summary": "Deals with moving bodies under the action of forces.",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "kinematics",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Kinematics",
                      "ta": "இயக்க விவரணவியல்"
                    },
                    "summary": "Motion is studied without considering its cause."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "kinetics",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Kinetics",
                      "ta": "இயக்க காரணவியல்"
                    },
                    "summary": "Motion is studied by considering the cause of motion."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "force-and-motion",
            "accent": "violet",
            "icon": "💪",
            "side": "left",
            "label": {
              "en": "Force & Motion",
              "ta": "விசையும் இயக்கமும்"
            },
            "summary": {
              "en": "Force is a push or pull that can change the state of motion of an object.",
              "ta": "ஒரு பொருளின் இயக்க நிலையை மாற்றக்கூடிய தள்ளுதல் அல்லது இழுத்தல் தான் விசை."
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "what-force-does",
                "label": {
                  "en": "What a Force Can Do",
                  "ta": "விசையின் விளைவுகள்"
                },
                "points": [
                  "Start the motion of a stationary body.",
                  "Stop a moving body.",
                  "Increase or decrease velocity.",
                  "Change the direction of motion."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "nature-of-force",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Nature of Force",
                  "ta": "விசையின் தன்மை"
                },
                "points": [
                  "Force is a vector quantity.",
                  "It has both magnitude and direction."
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "historical-ideas",
            "accent": "amber",
            "icon": "🏛️",
            "side": "left",
            "label": {
              "en": "Historical Ideas",
              "ta": "வரலாற்றுக் கருத்துக்கள்"
            },
            "summary": {
              "en": "How the understanding of force and motion grew from Aristotle to Galileo to Newton.",
              "ta": "அரிஸ்டாட்டில் முதல் நியூட்டன் வரை விசை மற்றும் இயக்கம் பற்றிய புரிதல் வளர்ந்த விதம்."
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "aristotle",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Aristotle",
                  "ta": "அரிஸ்டாட்டில்"
                },
                "summary": "Believed the natural state of earthly bodies is rest, and that force is required to maintain motion.",
                "points": [
                  "Natural state → Rest.",
                  "Moving bodies naturally come to rest.",
                  "Heavier objects fall faster than lighter objects.",
                  "Natural motion → force independent.",
                  "Violent motion → force dependent."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "galileo",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Galileo",
                  "ta": "கலிலியோ"
                },
                "summary": "Introduced the ideas that led towards the modern concept of inertia.",
                "points": [
                  "Natural state → Rest or uniform motion.",
                  "A moving body continues moving unless an external force acts.",
                  "Bodies resist changes in their state of motion — this resistance is inertia.",
                  "In vacuum, bodies of different masses fall at the same rate."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "concept-progression",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Concept Progression",
                  "ta": "கருத்து வளர்ச்சி"
                },
                "formula": "Aristotle → Galileo → Newton",
                "summary": "Rest as the natural state gave way to inertia, and inertia became Newton's First Law."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "inertia",
            "accent": "rose",
            "icon": "🛑",
            "side": "left",
            "label": {
              "en": "Inertia",
              "ta": "நிலைமம்"
            },
            "summary": {
              "en": "The tendency of a body to resist any change in its state of rest or uniform motion.",
              "ta": "ஓய்வு நிலையில் அல்லது சீரான இயக்கத்தில் உள்ள நிலையில் மாற்றத்தை எதிர்க்கும் பொருளின் தன்மை."
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "inertia-rest",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Inertia of Rest",
                  "ta": "ஓய்வு நிலைமம்"
                },
                "summary": "A body at rest tends to remain at rest.",
                "points": [
                  "A coin stays nearly at rest when the cardboard beneath it is flicked away."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "inertia-motion",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Inertia of Motion",
                  "ta": "இயக்க நிலைமம்"
                },
                "summary": "A moving body tends to continue moving.",
                "points": [
                  "An athlete runs before jumping to make a longer jump."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "inertia-direction",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Inertia of Direction",
                  "ta": "திசை நிலைமம்"
                },
                "summary": "A moving body tends to continue moving in the same direction.",
                "points": [
                  "A passenger leans sideways when a car takes a sharp turn."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "inertia-examples",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Everyday Examples",
                  "ta": "அன்றாட எடுத்துக்காட்டுகள்"
                },
                "points": [
                  "A passenger leans forward when a moving bus suddenly stops.",
                  "A passenger leans backward when a stationary bus suddenly starts.",
                  "Leaves and fruits fall when tree branches are shaken."
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "linear-momentum",
            "accent": "emerald",
            "icon": "🏃",
            "side": "left",
            "label": {
              "en": "Linear Momentum",
              "ta": "நேர்கோட்டு உந்தம்"
            },
            "formula": "p = mv",
            "summary": {
              "en": "Linear momentum measures the quantity of motion carried by a moving body.",
              "ta": "இயங்கும் பொருள் கொண்டிருக்கும் இயக்கத்தின் அளவு நேர்கோட்டு உந்தம்."
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "momentum-formula",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Formula",
                  "ta": "சூத்திரம்"
                },
                "formula": "p = mv",
                "points": [
                  "p = linear momentum",
                  "m = mass",
                  "v = velocity"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "momentum-key-points",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Key Points",
                  "ta": "முக்கிய குறிப்புகள்"
                },
                "points": [
                  "Momentum increases when mass increases.",
                  "Momentum increases when velocity increases.",
                  "Its direction is the same as the direction of velocity.",
                  "Momentum is a vector quantity."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "momentum-units",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Units",
                  "ta": "அலகுகள்"
                },
                "points": [
                  "SI → kg m s⁻¹",
                  "CGS → g cm s⁻¹"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "types-of-forces",
            "accent": "cyan",
            "icon": "⚖️",
            "side": "right",
            "label": {
              "en": "Types & Resultant of Forces",
              "ta": "விசைகளின் வகைகள்"
            },
            "summary": {
              "en": "Forces are classified by direction, and several forces acting together can be replaced by one resultant force.",
              "ta": "விசைகள் திசையைப் பொறுத்து வகைப்படுகின்றன; பல விசைகளின் ஒட்டுமொத்த விளைவை ஒரே விளைவு விசையால் குறிக்கலாம்."
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "like-parallel",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Like Parallel Forces",
                  "ta": "ஒரே திசை இணை விசைகள்"
                },
                "formula": "F_net = F₁ + F₂",
                "summary": "Two or more parallel forces acting in the same direction."
              },
              {
                "id": "unlike-parallel",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Unlike Parallel Forces",
                  "ta": "எதிர்த்திசை இணை விசைகள்"
                },
                "formula": "F_net = F₁ − F₂",
                "summary": "Two or more parallel forces acting in opposite directions.",
                "points": [
                  "The resultant acts in the direction of the greater force."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "resultant-force",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Resultant Force",
                  "ta": "விளைவு விசை"
                },
                "summary": "The single force that represents the combined effect of all forces on a body — the vector sum of those forces.",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "balanced-forces",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Balanced Forces",
                      "ta": "சமன் விசைகள்"
                    },
                    "formula": "Resultant = 0",
                    "summary": "The body stays in equilibrium."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "unbalanced-forces",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Unbalanced Forces",
                      "ta": "சமனற்ற விசைகள்"
                    },
                    "formula": "Resultant ≠ 0",
                    "summary": "The motion of the body can change."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "equilibrant",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Equilibrant",
                      "ta": "சமநிலை விசை"
                    },
                    "summary": "A force equal in magnitude and opposite in direction to the resultant force, which brings the system into equilibrium."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "rotational-effect",
            "accent": "indigo",
            "icon": "🌀",
            "side": "right",
            "label": {
              "en": "Rotational Effect of Force",
              "ta": "விசையின் சுழற்சி விளைவு"
            },
            "summary": {
              "en": "A force can produce a turning effect about a fixed point or axis.",
              "ta": "ஒரு விசை நிலையான புள்ளி அல்லது அச்சை மையமாகக் கொண்டு திருப்பு விளைவை ஏற்படுத்தும்."
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "turning-effect",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Turning Effect",
                  "ta": "திருப்பு விளைவு"
                },
                "points": [
                  "Axis of rotation → the fixed axis about which an object rotates.",
                  "Point of rotation (pivot) → the fixed point about which an object turns.",
                  "A door turns more easily when force is applied farther from the hinges — which is why handles sit far from them."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "torque",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Moment of Force / Torque",
                  "ta": "முறுக்கு விசை"
                },
                "formula": "τ = F × d",
                "summary": "The turning effect of a force about a fixed point or axis.",
                "points": [
                  "τ = torque, F = force, d = perpendicular distance from the pivot to the line of action.",
                  "Torque is a vector quantity.",
                  "SI unit → N m"
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "torque-direction",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Direction of Torque",
                      "ta": "முறுக்கு விசையின் திசை"
                    },
                    "points": [
                      "Anticlockwise → positive",
                      "Clockwise → negative"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "couple",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Couple",
                  "ta": "இரட்டை விசை"
                },
                "formula": "M = F × S",
                "summary": "Two equal and opposite parallel forces acting at different points.",
                "points": [
                  "Resultant force = 0, so there is no translational motion.",
                  "It produces pure rotation.",
                  "F = one of the forces, S = perpendicular distance between their lines of action."
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "couple-examples",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Examples",
                      "ta": "எடுத்துக்காட்டுகள்"
                    },
                    "points": [
                      "Turning a tap.",
                      "Winding or unwinding a screw.",
                      "Spinning a top."
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "torque-applications",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Applications of Torque",
                  "ta": "முறுக்கு விசையின் பயன்பாடுகள்"
                },
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "gears",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Gears",
                      "ta": "பற்சக்கரங்கள்"
                    },
                    "summary": "Gears transfer power and can change rotational speed and torque."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "seesaw",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Seesaw",
                      "ta": "ஏற்ற இறக்கப் பலகை"
                    },
                    "summary": "Changing the distance from the fulcrum changes the torque — greater distance gives greater torque."
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "steering",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Steering Wheel",
                      "ta": "திசைச் சக்கரம்"
                    },
                    "summary": "Its large radius lets the driver produce a large torque with little effort."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "principle-of-moments",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Principle of Moments",
                  "ta": "திருப்புத்திறன் விதி"
                },
                "formula": "F₁d₁ = F₂d₂",
                "summary": "For a body in rotational equilibrium, the total clockwise moment equals the total anticlockwise moment.",
                "points": [
                  "Equilibrium condition → the sum of all moments is zero."
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "newtons-laws",
            "accent": "teal",
            "icon": "📜",
            "side": "right",
            "label": {
              "en": "Newton's Laws",
              "ta": "நியூட்டனின் விதிகள்"
            },
            "summary": {
              "en": "Three laws that tie force to inertia, to acceleration, and to the equal and opposite reaction.",
              "ta": "விசையை நிலைமம், முடுக்கம் மற்றும் எதிர்வினையுடன் இணைக்கும் மூன்று விதிகள்."
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "first-law",
                "label": {
                  "en": "First Law — Law of Inertia",
                  "ta": "முதல் விதி — நிலைம விதி"
                },
                "summary": "A body remains at rest or continues in uniform motion in a straight line unless acted upon by an external unbalanced force.",
                "points": [
                  "No net force → no change in motion.",
                  "Explains inertia, rest, uniform motion, and the need for an external force to change motion."
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "second-law",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Second Law — Law of Force",
                  "ta": "இரண்டாம் விதி — விசை விதி"
                },
                "formula": "F = Δp / t  →  F = ma",
                "summary": "The force acting on a body is proportional to the rate of change of its linear momentum.",
                "points": [
                  "Greater force → greater acceleration.",
                  "Greater mass → smaller acceleration for the same force."
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "units-of-force",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Units of Force",
                      "ta": "விசையின் அலகுகள்"
                    },
                    "formula": "1 N = 10⁵ dyne",
                    "points": [
                      "SI → newton (N); 1 N = 1 kg m s⁻²",
                      "CGS → dyne; 1 dyne = 1 g cm s⁻²"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "gravitational-units",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Gravitational Unit of Force",
                      "ta": "விசையின் ஈர்ப்பு அலகு"
                    },
                    "points": [
                      "SI → kilogram-force (kgf); 1 kgf = 9.8 N",
                      "CGS → gram-force (gf); 1 gf = 980 dyne"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "impulse",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Impulse",
                  "ta": "உந்துவிசை"
                },
                "formula": "J = F × t = Δp",
                "summary": "The product of a force and the time for which it acts — equal to the change in momentum.",
                "points": [
                  "Units → N s or kg m s⁻¹"
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "impulse-applications",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Applications",
                      "ta": "பயன்பாடுகள்"
                    },
                    "points": [
                      "Shock absorbers increase the stopping time and so reduce the force felt.",
                      "A cricket fielder pulls the hands backward while catching, increasing stopping time and reducing the force on the hands."
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "third-law",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Third Law — Action & Reaction",
                  "ta": "மூன்றாம் விதி — வினையும் எதிர்வினையும்"
                },
                "formula": "Fᴮ = −Fᴬ",
                "summary": "For every action there is an equal and opposite reaction, and the two forces act on different bodies.",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "third-law-examples",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Examples",
                      "ta": "எடுத்துக்காட்டுகள்"
                    },
                    "points": [
                      "🐦 A flying bird pushes air downward; the air pushes the bird upward.",
                      "🏊 A swimmer pushes water backward; the water pushes the swimmer forward.",
                      "🔫 A bullet moves forward; the gun recoils backward."
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "conservation-momentum",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Conservation of Linear Momentum",
                  "ta": "நேர்கோட்டு உந்த அழிவின்மை"
                },
                "formula": "m₁u₁ + m₂u₂ = m₁v₁ + m₂v₂",
                "summary": "The total linear momentum of a system stays constant when no net external force acts on it.",
                "points": [
                  "Before collision → m₁u₁ + m₂u₂",
                  "After collision → m₁v₁ + m₂v₂"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "rocket-propulsion",
                "label": {
                  "en": "Rocket Propulsion",
                  "ta": "ராக்கெட் இயக்கம்"
                },
                "summary": "Rockets fly by Newton's Third Law together with conservation of linear momentum.",
                "points": [
                  "Fuel burns → hot gases are expelled at high speed.",
                  "The backward momentum of the gases produces an equal and opposite reaction.",
                  "The rocket moves forward; as fuel is used its mass falls and its velocity rises."
                ],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "escape-velocity",
                    "label": {
                      "en": "Escape Velocity",
                      "ta": "விடுபடு திசைவேகம்"
                    },
                    "summary": "The velocity an object needs in order to escape the Earth's gravitational pull."
                  }
